  <div>
    <a href="/" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300 text-sm">← Obelo</a>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">Last updated: June 2026</p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">What Obelo is</h2>
      <p>Obelo is a self-hosted personal productivity application run by the person or organisation that hosts this server (the server operator). It is not a public service unless the operator says so.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">Data we collect</h2>
      <p>Obelo stores the data you explicitly enter: your account information (username, display name, email address), notes, tasks, reminders, routines, lists, and calendar connections.</p>
      <p>We also store application logs for diagnostic purposes. Logs record actions (e.g. login events, errors) but do not include the content of your personal data.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">How your data is used</h2>
      <p>Your data is used solely to provide the Obelo service to you. It is not sold, shared with third parties, or used for advertising.</p>
      <p>If you connect Google Calendar, Obelo accesses your calendar data to display and create events within the app. This data is stored locally on the server and is not shared with any third party.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">Google Calendar data</h2>
      <p>Obelo's use of data obtained from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300 underline">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>
      <p>Calendar data accessed via Google is used only to display your events within Obelo and to create events on your behalf when you use the calendar feature. It is not used for any other purpose and is not shared with third parties.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">Data storage</h2>
      <p>All data is stored on the server run by the server operator. Data does not leave this server except where you explicitly connect a third-party service (e.g. Google Calendar, Apple CalDAV).</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">Server operator access</h2>
      <p>As the server operator, the operator has administrative access to the underlying infrastructure. The application is designed so that the admin interface does not expose individual users' personal data. Users are protected from each other at the application level.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">Data retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>Your data is retained for as long as your account is active. You may request deletion of your account and all associated data by contacting the server operator directly.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy can be directed to the server operator, using the contact details they provide.</p>
    </section>

